 "scope_id": "COUNT-TFNP-20261107-001",
 "title": "The knot sphere's count is PPADS-complete, and its orientation is what keeps it out of PPAD",
 "subject": "Which decision-tree TFNP class the knot sphere's count belongs to, and whether it has low-degree Nullstellensatz refutations",
 "conclusion": "Finding a violated line of the octahedral knot sphere is PPADS^dt-complete and lies outside PPAD^dt, PPA^dt and PLS^dt, so its not-all-equal formula has no polylogarithmic-degree Nullstellensatz refutation over F2 or in unary form although unary Sherali-Adams refutes it at degree 3. Counting monochromatic faces as solutions too, the count becomes PPAD^dt-complete, so the knot's orientation alone separates the two classes.",
